{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01267",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 1.05,
      "end_seconds": 6.14,
      "duration_seconds": 5.09,
      "text": "Hi, sit anywhere you like. Did the receptionist sort you out quickly?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 7.07,
      "end_seconds": 10.47,
      "duration_seconds": 3.4,
      "text": "Yes, she was lovely about it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 11.81,
      "end_seconds": 14.43,
      "duration_seconds": 2.62,
      "text": "Tell me what's brought you in."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 16.08,
      "end_seconds": 22.01,
      "duration_seconds": 5.93,
      "text": "um, so... a cut on my finger. That's why I came"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 32.98,
      "end_seconds": 36.28,
      "duration_seconds": 3.3,
      "text": "When was the first time you noticed it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 37.87,
      "end_seconds": 40.5,
      "duration_seconds": 2.63,
      "text": "About... well, about two weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 42.48,
      "end_seconds": 44.15,
      "duration_seconds": 1.67,
      "text": "Anything that improves it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 45.85,
      "end_seconds": 49.75,
      "duration_seconds": 3.9,
      "text": "only a dressing, and it's not much"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 51.48,
      "end_seconds": 53.58,
      "duration_seconds": 2.1,
      "text": "Have you noticed any triggers?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 54.23,
      "end_seconds": 79.21,
      "duration_seconds": 24.98,
      "text": "Yes, gripping. That makes it worse. As for pain in the finger, I honestly can't say when that began. It might have been last month or the month before. Right, about pain in the finger, it's severe, honestly. Oh, there's difficulty bending the finger as well."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 80.96,
      "end_seconds": 85.39,
      "duration_seconds": 4.43,
      "text": "and what about dirt in the wound or redness spreading?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 87.44,
      "end_seconds": 90.36,
      "duration_seconds": 2.92,
      "text": "No, none of those at all."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 91.28,
      "end_seconds": 95.97,
      "duration_seconds": 4.69,
      "text": "Any weakness of the hand, pus or fever at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 96.65,
      "end_seconds": 99.46,
      "duration_seconds": 2.81,
      "text": "No, none of those at all."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 100.78,
      "end_seconds": 103.85,
      "duration_seconds": 3.07,
      "text": "Alright, any trouble with the waterworks?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 104.93,
      "end_seconds": 106.42,
      "duration_seconds": 1.49,
      "text": "No changes there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 108.06,
      "end_seconds": 110.28,
      "duration_seconds": 2.22,
      "text": "Your breathing, any trouble there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 110.8,
      "end_seconds": 112.96,
      "duration_seconds": 2.16,
      "text": "No problems with breathing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 130.2,
      "end_seconds": 134.73,
      "duration_seconds": 4.53,
      "text": "Can you list what you take, tablets, creams or inhalers?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 135.7,
      "end_seconds": 143.18,
      "duration_seconds": 7.48,
      "text": "Glycomet. I take it 500 milligrams, twice a day. Metoprolol. I take it twice a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 143.69,
      "end_seconds": 145.96,
      "duration_seconds": 2.27,
      "text": "And what strength is that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 146.84,
      "end_seconds": 151.67,
      "duration_seconds": 4.83,
      "text": "50 milligrams, I think that's what's on the box"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 153.57,
      "end_seconds": 155.86,
      "duration_seconds": 2.29,
      "text": "Right, and for how long?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 157.24,
      "end_seconds": 159.33,
      "duration_seconds": 2.09,
      "text": "About about three months."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 160.84,
      "end_seconds": 163.64,
      "duration_seconds": 2.8,
      "text": "Have you ever had an operation?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 164.8,
      "end_seconds": 169.92,
      "duration_seconds": 5.12,
      "text": "Yes, I had a triple bypass, eight years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 171.03,
      "end_seconds": 174.02,
      "duration_seconds": 2.99,
      "text": "are there any illnesses in your family?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 174.69,
      "end_seconds": 177.11,
      "duration_seconds": 2.42,
      "text": "My aunt has rheumatoid arthritis."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 179.05,
      "end_seconds": 183.01,
      "duration_seconds": 3.96,
      "text": "are there any allergies I should be aware of?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 184.49,
      "end_seconds": 189.71,
      "duration_seconds": 5.22,
      "text": "Okay, so yes, grass pollen, it gives me itchy eyes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 191.32,
      "end_seconds": 195.71,
      "duration_seconds": 4.39,
      "text": "anything in your past medical history I should know?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 197.39,
      "end_seconds": 201.19,
      "duration_seconds": 3.8,
      "text": "Yes, diabetes. I've had heart disease, yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 201.74,
      "end_seconds": 211.91,
      "duration_seconds": 10.17,
      "text": "Okay, I can see diabetes in your file as well. Tell me about your routine, work, habits, that sort of thing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 212.47,
      "end_seconds": 232.18,
      "duration_seconds": 19.71,
      "text": "No, I've never smoked in my life. I only drink at family occasions. I'm a plumber, lots of bending and kneeling. Not much, I mostly stay in these days. I grab fast food at lunch most days"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 234.95,
      "end_seconds": 237.91,
      "duration_seconds": 2.96,
      "text": "Okay, time for me to examine you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 239.53,
      "end_seconds": 242.06,
      "duration_seconds": 2.53,
      "text": "I'll listen to your chest now"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 250.22,
      "end_seconds": 258.38,
      "duration_seconds": 8.16,
      "text": "there is a two-centimetre clean cut over the first knuckle, the finger moves fully and the fingertip feels normal"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 264.1,
      "end_seconds": 266.58,
      "duration_seconds": 2.48,
      "text": "Thank you, you can get dressed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 278.19,
      "end_seconds": 288.21,
      "duration_seconds": 10.02,
      "text": "Right, here's what I'm thinking. I'd lean towards a clean finger laceration without nerve or tendon injury. An infected wound is also on my list."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 293.19,
      "end_seconds": 295.26,
      "duration_seconds": 2.07,
      "text": "Is this serious, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 296.32,
      "end_seconds": 317.04,
      "duration_seconds": 20.72,
      "text": "I can't promise yet, but most people with a clean finger laceration without nerve or tendon injury do well once it's treated properly. Just to be sure I understood. You've had a cut on your finger for about two weeks, and no dirt in the wound or weakness of the hand"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 318.11,
      "end_seconds": 319.77,
      "duration_seconds": 1.66,
      "text": "That's it, yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 321.52,
      "end_seconds": 326.65,
      "duration_seconds": 5.13,
      "text": "Let's book an X-ray of the finger to look into laceration."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 327.2,
      "end_seconds": 329.71,
      "duration_seconds": 2.51,
      "text": "Do I need to prepare?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 330.87,
      "end_seconds": 356.05,
      "duration_seconds": 25.18,
      "text": "I'll start you on tetanus booster, 0.5 ml, once, for one day it's for tetanus prevention it's a a commonly used medicine and most people tolerate it well keep the dressing dry for two days and watch for redness or pus see me again if it looks infected before we finish, can you repeat the plan back to me?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 357.8,
      "end_seconds": 369.3,
      "duration_seconds": 11.5,
      "text": "so, I take the tetanus booster, 0.5 ml, once and come back if it looks infected is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 370.71,
      "end_seconds": 377.08,
      "duration_seconds": 6.37,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. Right, that's the plan. Do you want to to ask me anything?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 378.67,
      "end_seconds": 383.44,
      "duration_seconds": 4.77,
      "text": "Okay, um, so alright, thanks, take care."
    }
  ]
}